This marker is repeated at directory level because GitHub's licence detector
reads only the repository root LICENSE, which is MIT for the code. Without this
file, every summary here would be presented as MIT-licensed software, which is
both wrong and legible as wrong to the people most likely to read it.

The authoritative path-to-licence map is ../COPYRIGHT.md.

Note what this does NOT license: the papers being summarised. Each summary is
my own description of someone else's work, and copyright in that work remains
with its authors and publisher.
